# Rocket-Powered Goblin Glider: "When this Equipment enters, if it was cast from your graveyard, attach it to target creature
# you control." A card in a graveyard is in its owner's (CR 404.1), so a Glider cast from an opponent's graveyard was not cast
# from yours, even though you cast it. Bot2 loots its Glider away with Faithless Looting on turn 2. On turn 3 Bot1's
# Tinybones hits Bot2 and Bot1 casts the Glider from Bot2's graveyard, paying {3} with three Moxen. It enters under Bot1's
# control and does not trigger: it is not attached, and Tinybones stays a 1/1 without flying.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Tinybones, the Pickpocket
Plains x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Faithless Looting
Rocket-Powered Goblin Glider
Island x17

